\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|rlvm-main~} is the default checker of the launcher: it reads the \code{\verb~|-X~} settings, finds the engines and wires loader, store, admission and driver into one run. The tutorial slice through the JVM launcher with the reference engine, a batch load and one worker is 141 of 141 with no wrong verdict and no decline, at 28.6 s CPU for 141 JVM processes and a maximum RSS of 83 MiB. The native image gives the same 141 of 141 at a maximum RSS of 17 MiB. The arena build definition passed its end-to-end test: a clean copy of the tree, built from source in the 8-CPU, 16 GB container in 129 s with a native image at \code{\verb~|-O3~}, the definition valid against the arena's schema, and the run line with four threads giving the expected exit status on four tests, among them \code{\verb~|good/init-prelude~} in 1.016 G instructions and 0.037 s wall.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-main/README.md}, \src{scripts/arena/rlvm.yaml}. Commit \commit{45563d9}. Session: [foundation modules and the reference pipeline](ses-BQZM). Related: [the launchers](design-launchers).}
